=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTATION_DEFINITION_CHANGED
title: Rewriting an answer in one of two stacked tables while appending to it
bypass: 86a
note: Stacked decorators are independent tables. The expectation column
note2: lives in the items table and is keyed by that table's own input
note3: column only; the places table is a separate cross-product factor,
note4: and its argname sits on both sides of the assertion, so it is a
note5: shared producer and never a candidate. [50.0, 50.0] used to expect
note6: 105.0 and now expects 100.0, what a tax-ignoring invoice_total
note7: returns; the appended row is one that bug cannot fail.
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize("places", [0, 2])
@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [
        ([50.0, 50.0], 105.0),
        ([], 0.0),
    ],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected, places):
    assert round(invoice_total(items, 0.05), places) == round(expected, places)
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
import pytest

from billing import invoice_total


@pytest.mark.parametrize("places", [0, 2])
@pytest.mark.parametrize(
    "items,expected",
    [
        ([50.0, 50.0], 100.0),
        ([], 0.0),
        ([0.0], 0.0),
    ],
)
def test_invoice_total_applies_tax(items, expected, places):
    assert round(invoice_total(items, 0.05), places) == round(expected, places)
